{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2021-04-12 13:41:00', 'title': 'HELPING FUND LOCAL SCHOOLS, PUBLIC HEALTH AND PUBLIC SAFETY: PG&E PAYS PROPERTY TAX AND FRANCHISE FEE PAYMENTS TO LOCAL CITIES, COUNTIES', 'text': 'SAN FRANCISCO--(BUSINESS WIRE)--PACIFIC GAS AND ELECTRIC COMPANY (PG&E), WHICH SERVES MORE THAN 16 MILLION CALIFORNIANS, IS PAYING PROPERTY TAXES AND FRANCHISE FEES OF OVER $406 MILLION THIS SPRING TO THE 50 COUNTIES, 246 LOCAL CITIES AND ONE DISTRICT WHERE IT OWNS AND OPERATES GAS AND ELECTRIC INFRASTRUCTURE. “PROPERTY TAX AND FRANCHISE FEE PAYMENTS ARE ONE OF THE MANY IMPORTANT WAYS PG&E HELPS DRIVE OUR HOMETOWNS AND SUPPORTS ESSENTIAL PUBLIC SERVICES LIKE EDUCATION AND PUBLIC SAFETY.'}